\fs28 \cf0 ##HIGH-END FASHION
\fs24  \
\
\
Heritage, Craft, and Innovation\
.\
High-end characteristics:\
\
\'95Innovative materials: gazar, organza, bonded silk, structured wool\
\'95Architectural construction: internal structure, interlining, horsehair braid\
\'95Complex paneling: godets, engineered flare, sculptural hems\
\'95Artistic narrative: references to YSL, couture archives, 1950s silhouettes\
\'95Low production volumes: hand finishing, couture craftsmanship\
\
Examples:\
\
\'95Dior / YSL Heritage: dramatic trapeze flare with couture structure.\
\'95Comme des Gar\'e7ons: exaggerated geometric panels.\
\'95Maison Margiela: deconstructed trapeze volumes.\
\
High-end trapeze skirts act as wearable architecture.\
\
High-End Fashion: Concept, Craftsmanship, and Innovation\
\
In the luxury segment, trapeze skirts often serve as a canvas for craftsmanship, sculptural form, and experimentation. High-end brands prioritize:\
\
\'95Innovative materials: bonded fabrics, neoprene, organza, technical wools, treated leather\
\'95Architectural tailoring: draping, asymmetric panels, sculptural volumes\
\'95Artistic storytelling and runway context: garments often appear as conceptual pieces rather than everyday items\
\'95Limited production and hand-finishing: emphasizing quality and uniqueness\
Luxury trapeze skirts often prioritize artistic expression over practicality, existing at the intersection of fashion and art.
